(A) Use water and release carbon - This is incorrect because plants do not primarily use water to release carbon. Instead, they use water in photosynthesis.

(B) Use sugar and release carbon - This is also incorrect. Plants do not primarily use sugar to release carbon; rather, they break down sugar through respiration, which can release carbon dioxide.

(C) Use carbon and release oxygen - This is correct. During photosynthesis, plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and use it along with sunlight and water to produce glucose (a type of sugar) and oxygen. The overall equation for photosynthesis is:
\[ 6CO_2 + 6H_2O + \text{light energy} \rightarrow C_6H_{12}O_6 + 6O_2 \]
So, plants use carbon dioxide and release oxygen.

(D) Use carbon and release nitrogen - This is incorrect. Plants do not primarily use carbon to release nitrogen. Nitrogen fixation is typically performed by certain bacteria, not plants.

