(A) **the ability of the snake to survive to reproduce**: In evolutionary terms, traits that enhance survival and reproduction are more likely to be passed on to future generations. If the white-spotted pattern helps the snake survive better or attract mates more effectively, it is more likely to become common.

(B) **the appearance of other new traits in the baby snake**: This is less relevant to the spread of the white-spotted pattern. The emergence of other traits does not directly influence the frequency of the white-spotted pattern unless they somehow interact with it.

